Future Enhancements
While the current implementation demonstrates a functional security monitoring framework, several enhancements can further improve the platform's capabilities:
Advanced AI-Based Detection
* Deploy deep learning models such as LSTM and Transformer architectures for time-series anomaly detection.
* Implement predictive maintenance using telemetry trends and historical equipment behavior.
* Introduce adaptive risk scoring that learns from previous incidents.
Digital Twin Integration
* Develop a real-time digital twin of the printer and manufacturing environment.
* Compare expected behavior against actual machine behavior to identify deviations instantly.
* Simulate attacks and process failures before physical production begins.
Blockchain and Traceability
* Integrate Hyperledger Fabric or enterprise blockchain platforms.
* Store immutable records of design approvals, print events, and security incidents.
* Enable end-to-end part provenance and compliance auditing.
Enterprise SIEM Integration
* Forward security events to enterprise platforms such as Splunk, ELK Stack, Wazuh, or Microsoft Sentinel.
* Support Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response (SOAR) workflows.
* Enable centralized monitoring across multiple manufacturing facilities.
Zero Trust Manufacturing
* Extend device authentication using hardware-rooted identities and PUF-based trust mechanisms.
* Implement continuous authorization and least-privilege access controls.
* Integrate with NIST Zero Trust Architecture principles.
Industrial IoT Expansion
* Support multiple printers and production lines simultaneously.
* Collect telemetry from additional Industrial IoT sensors.
* Build plant-wide security visibility and anomaly detection.
Cloud-Native Deployment
* Containerize monitoring services using Docker.
* Deploy scalable microservices on Kubernetes.
* Enable high availability and distributed manufacturing environments.
Regulatory Compliance
* Align security controls with:
   * NIST SP 800-207 (Zero Trust)
   * NIST SP 800-53
   * IEC 62443
   * ISO 27001
   * Aerospace and Medical Manufacturing Standards
